=========================================================
MOST ASKED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
=========================================================

Q1. Difference between Association and Aggregation?

Association:
General relationship with no ownership.

Aggregation:
Special type of association with weak ownership.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Difference between Aggregation and Composition?

Aggregation:
Weak ownership.
Child can exist independently.

Composition:
Strong ownership.
Child is destroyed with parent.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Difference between Composition and Inheritance?

Composition:
HAS-A relationship.
Preferred for flexibility and loose coupling.

Inheritance:
IS-A relationship.
Used only when a true inheritance hierarchy exists.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What is Dependency?

A temporary USES relationship where one class depends on another without owning it.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. What is Realization?

A relationship where a class implements an interface or abstract class.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Which relationship is preferred in modern software design?

Composition

Reason:
• Low coupling
• High cohesion
• Better maintainability
• Better flexibility
• Easier testing

